vpn-manager (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of VPN Manager: the per-user WireGuard client migrated from
    a per-user WireGuard client for Debian GNOME, written as VpnManager.* on
    Core v0.2.1.
  * NetworkManager is the connection engine; the application never elevates and
    never reads or writes /etc/wireguard.
  * Profiles are read no-follow and bounded, validated before they reach
    NetworkManager, and written atomically owner-only.
  * The package applies only its own sysctl drop-in on install.

 -- Younes Benmoussa <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0000
